Z||000000||Black88GT||03-29-2001||01:55 PM||||I am about ready to up and buy a Mac.  Windows has put me over the edge.  <P>OK I figured out why I was running compatibility mode, I fixed that.  So I thought everything would be OK.  Wrong.  I was still getting all the error messages I was before, only in KERNELL32.DLL and MSHTML.DLL though.  So I go to turn on my computer and it says "Windows has encountered an error accessing your system registry, Windows will restart and repair the system registry".  SO I hit OK and it restarts.  Well, it keeps on giving me this message no matter how many times I restart.  I can still do things obviously but I have that message on my screen still.  Is there anyway to fix this without reformatting and reinstalling Winblows?  I have done this over 10 times and it gets very frustrating going through the process once or twice a month.  I even bought a CD-R just so I could backup my files for the reformat/reinstallation.<P><BR>TIA for any help<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Raydar||03-29-2001||02:05 PM||||Try reinstalling Windows over the existing setup, without reformatting. I have successfully fixed strange stuff by doing that. Should leave most if not all of your data and apps intact.<BR>This doesn't address why it keeps breaking, but it may save you some time with the rest of it.<BR>If all you have is a recovery disk, instead of a real Windows disk, then this probably won't do you any good.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
